!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section HNO3: HNO3 + hv --> OH + NO2
! source : JPL-2006
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Nitrogen acids" -> "HONO2" -> "JPL-2006"
! Quantum yield = 1
! Temperature dep. according to the relation:
!   crs(wl,T) = crs(wl,298) exp(B(wl)*1.e-3 * (T-298))
!   where B is the parameter found below in the last column
! Rem: JPL-2006 reports other values of q.y. and considers varisous branchs
!   in addition to OH + NO2. However, since these data are given for only
!   specific wl, q.y. is thus fixed to unity (crs-2004) by following
!   JPL-1997 and Johnston et al.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        56  | Finishes at wl interval :  102
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
